note ===== fts.om : SQLite 3.45.0 FTS5 replica for cortex-rs search_entities =====
note Owner FtsEngine. Globals q*, functions fts_*.
note Replicates, for the table
note   entities_fts USING fts5(id UNINDEXED, canonical_name, content, space_slug UNINDEXED)
note and the statement
note   SELECT .. COALESCE(bm25(entities_fts), 5.0) AS bm25_rank FROM entities e
note   JOIN entities_fts f ON f.id = e.id WHERE entities_fts MATCH ?1 AND e.space_slug = ?2
note   AND e.retracted = 0 ORDER BY bm25_rank ASC LIMIT ?3
note what SQLite 3.45.0 (libsqlite3-sys 0.28.0, gcc -O3 as built into cortex-rs) returns:
note the FTS5 expression grammar (Lemon tables of fts5parse.y), the parse actions of
note fts5_expr.c, the node iteration engine (TERM, STRING/NEAR, AND, OR, NOT, colsets, ^, *),
note the position lists the xInst API exposes, bm25 with k1=1.2 b=0.75 in the exact floating
note operation order (pairwise vector loop, fused last term) of fts5Bm25Function, the plan
note SCAN f (rowid ascending) + SEARCH e + temp b-tree ORDER BY with LIMIT (stable on ties).
note
note API (callers write the input globals, then call)
note   fts_init                  once (idempotent; also run by fts_put/fts_search)
note   fts_put doc row -> bool   add FTS row `row` (the entities_fts rowid) for doc slot `doc`
note                             (< 4194304), columns canonical_name = qnm[0..qnml),
note                             content = qct[0..qctl). A doc slot already present is deleted
note                             first (cortex-rs does DELETE then INSERT). false: row already
note                             used by another doc, or a capacity limit (see below) was hit.
note   fts_del doc               remove the FTS row of doc slot `doc` (no-op when absent)
note   fts_reset                 drop every row
note   fts_search -> ulong       MATCH string qq[0..qql) (SQLite reads it up to the first NUL),
note                             join filter qok[doc] = 1 when entities e (e.id = f.id) has the
note                             wanted space_slug and retracted = 0, LIMIT qlim. Returns the
note                             row count n; qrd[0..n) doc slots and qrb[0..n) bm25_rank in
note                             SQL output order. qerr = 1 when SQLite would raise an error
note                             (syntax error, unknown column, ...; cortex-rs then sees 0 rows),
note                             2 when a capacity limit of this replica was hit (0 rows).
note   fts_rows / fts_tokens     nRow and total token count (the bm25 table statistics)
note Capacities: 4194304 doc slots, 16777216 token words, 2097152 distinct terms (16 MiB of
note term bytes), 8388608 posting entries per query batch, 65536 query terms/phrases/nodes,
note 1048576 result rows (qlim is clamped to that).
note generated by tests/fts/gen_parse_tables.py from sqlite3.c sha256 7956a38f236a6be6c0bb30c96ba4f85f19e5a69f6beb6d2c62c9d246972a6775 (SQLite 3.45.0)
const QPA ulong 0
const QPL ulong 105
const QPS ulong 226
const QPR ulong 261
const QPD ulong 279
const QPH ulong 314
const QPN ulong 342
const QPT ulong 370
text qptx "81 20 96 6 28 99 98 26 26 18 96 6 28 17 98 56 26 19 96 6 28 14 98 14 26 31 92 96 6 28 108 98 25 26 21 96 6 28 78 98 58 26 29 96 6 28 107 98 22 26 24 16 12 11 1 13 13 24 16 23 11 33 34 13 97 8 27 32 98 7 26 3 4 5 3 4 5 3 83 4 5 3 63 5 3 62 12 2 86 13 9 30 10 10 54 57 75 78 78 53 57 15 82 82 71 16 17 18 19 20 22 22 24 24 17 18 19 20 7 22 9 24 17 18 19 20 9 22 9 24 13 17 18 19 20 26 22 24 24 17 18 19 20 15 22 9 24 17 18 19 20 26 22 21 24 6 7 9 9 10 12 12 6 7 21 9 24 25 12 18 5 20 14 22 5 24 3 1 2 3 1 2 3 0 1 2 3 11 2 3 11 9 10 5 12 23 24 10 10 8 9 9 15 15 8 9 9 27 27 11 27 27 27 27 27 27 27 27 27 27 27 27 27 27 27 27 44 44 44 44 44 44 51 77 43 12 14 83 82 14 23 23 31 31 71 74 78 81 86 91 6 53 53 60 64 68 53 87 92 53 93 84 92 100 109 117 125 146 83 83 137 167 104 104 108 104 120 127 138 80 80 80 80 80 80 95 80 80 105 80 110 110 80 110 110 80 80 80 80 80 91 80 80 80 101 100 80 80 90 103 80 80 104 80 16 20 20 20 20 21 21 17 17 17 17 17 17 19 19 18 18 22 22 22 23 23 25 25 24 24 26 26 1 4 3 1 2 2 1 3 3 3 5 3 1 1 2 1 3 1 2 5 1 2 0 2 4 2 1 0"
text qcolx "id canonical_name content space_slug"
const QD ulong 4194304
const QTKN ulong 16777216
const QTM ulong 2097152
const QTH ulong 4194304
const QTB ulong 16777216
const QE ulong 8388608
const QA ulong 4194304
const QX ulong 65536
const QR ulong 1048576
note --- storage ---
global qdrow ulong QD
global qdst uint QD
global qsr uint QD
global qsn ulong 1
global qtot ulong 1
